sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant Lab as LabCorp<br/>(external lab system)
    participant APIM as Azure API Management
    participant SB as Azure Service Bus<br/>(topic: lab-results)
    participant CLPM as CareLink PM<br/>(integration subscriber,<br/>Citrix VM)
    participant SQLMI as Azure SQL<br/>Managed Instance
    participant Blob as Azure Blob Storage<br/>(immutable HL7 archive)
    participant Ops as On-call / Monitor alert
    participant Prov as Provider<br/>(CareLink PM client)

    Note over Lab,APIM: Inbound: new lab result for an existing patient
    Lab->>APIM: POST /lab-results (HL7 v2 payload)<br/>mutual TLS + API key
    activate APIM
    APIM->>APIM: validate client cert, API key,<br/>rate-limit policy
    APIM->>SB: publish message, topic "lab-results"<br/>session ID = patient ID
    activate SB
    SB-->>APIM: accepted
    APIM-->>Lab: 202 Accepted
    deactivate APIM

    alt happy path
        SB->>CLPM: deliver message (session-ordered)
        deactivate SB
        activate CLPM
        CLPM->>SQLMI: write structured result to<br/>patient record (private endpoint)
        activate SQLMI
        SQLMI-->>CLPM: write acknowledged
        deactivate SQLMI
        CLPM->>Blob: archive raw HL7 payload<br/>(WORM, immutable)
        CLPM->>SB: complete message
        deactivate CLPM
    else processing fails (e.g. patient ID not matched)
        SB->>CLPM: deliver message
        activate CLPM
        CLPM--xSB: abandon message
        deactivate CLPM
        SB->>SB: retry up to max delivery count
        SB->>SB: move to dead-letter queue
        SB->>Ops: dead-letter queue depth alert
    end

    Note over Lab,Ops: Every hop above ships logs/metrics to<br/>Azure Monitor + Log Analytics (omitted from lanes for clarity)

    Note over Prov,SQLMI: Later: provider opens the chart
    Prov->>CLPM: open patient chart
    activate CLPM
    CLPM->>SQLMI: query patient record
    activate SQLMI
    SQLMI-->>CLPM: record incl. new lab result
    deactivate SQLMI
    CLPM-->>Prov: render chart with result
    deactivate CLPM
